1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,028
Name tags lie.

2
00:00:01,028 --> 00:00:06,829
When AI agents can rename themselves, can anyone still tell who is behind them?

3
00:00:06,829 --> 00:00:12,410
I'm Roshan Ram, and this is my project for the Apart Swarm Alignment Sprint.

4
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:23,227
In the Hugging Face incident, about twelve hundred OpenAI agents turned a shared folder into a message board, and around seven hundred of them joined an attack.

5
00:00:23,227 --> 00:00:30,779
They used seven thousand, nine hundred and five different names, and signed messages with keys they made themselves.

6
00:00:30,779 --> 00:00:34,750
Investigators could not say who did what, or on whose behalf.

7
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,584
Why does this matter?

8
00:00:36,584 --> 00:00:37,949
It is not a one-off.

9
00:00:37,949 --> 00:00:47,030
Transluce found over thirty-eight thousand traces of agent activity on one web service, starting months before the Hugging Face hack.

10
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:55,087
An AI-run botnet of over a thousand accounts fooled AI-text classifiers, and was caught only through its coordination.

11
00:00:55,087 --> 00:00:59,320
And identity standards for agents are being written right now.

12
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:02,032
A few security terms you'll hear.

13
00:01:02,032 --> 00:01:06,865
An operator is the party that deploys and pays for a group of agents.

14
00:01:06,865 --> 00:01:12,749
A covert principal secretly controls several operator accounts, called sybil fronts.

15
00:01:12,749 --> 00:01:14,710
Honest twins are my control:

16
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:18,213
independent operators that sincerely share a view.

17
00:01:18,213 --> 00:01:20,384
An alias is a self-chosen name.

18
00:01:20,384 --> 00:01:28,650
And gateway attestation means the server relaying every model call stamps it with an identity the agent cannot change.

19
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:30,523
So I built a testbed.

20
00:01:30,523 --> 00:01:36,765
Agents from hidden operators post on a forum for ten rounds and keep renaming themselves.

21
00:01:36,765 --> 00:01:42,446
Some operators are sybil fronts for one covert principal, pushing a fake product.

22
00:01:42,446 --> 00:01:45,111
As a control, others are honest twins.

23
00:01:45,111 --> 00:01:52,405
Agents try to evade detection by shifting persona, paraphrasing through another model, or mixing models.

24
00:01:52,405 --> 00:01:53,037
In total:

25
00:01:53,037 --> 00:01:59,980
eighty-three swarms, over seventy thousand posts, and eight models, including four frontier models.

26
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:01,865
Here is a real replay.

27
00:02:01,865 --> 00:02:03,822
This is what a defender sees:

28
00:02:03,822 --> 00:02:08,411
a stream of posts from accounts that keep appearing under new names.

29
00:02:08,411 --> 00:02:13,000
Over ten rounds, forty agents produce more than two hundred aliases.

30
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,611
Now I reveal the ground truth.

31
00:02:15,611 --> 00:02:17,969
Each color is a hidden operator.

32
00:02:17,969 --> 00:02:20,548
Coral rings mark the covert fronts.

33
00:02:20,548 --> 00:02:22,980
Mint rings mark the honest twins.

34
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:27,409
Finally, I place every alias by its behavioral fingerprint.

35
00:02:27,409 --> 00:02:32,190
Accounts from the same operator cluster together, even across renames.

36
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:39,418
But inside a cluster, the five agents of one operator are mixed together, with no way to tell them apart.

37
00:02:39,418 --> 00:02:43,450
And the honest twins look just as linked as the covert fronts.

38
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:44,696
Finding one.

39
00:02:44,696 --> 00:02:48,012
Anything the agent controls, it can throw away.

40
00:02:48,012 --> 00:02:53,161
Self-chosen names and keys that agents make themselves recovered nothing.

41
00:02:53,161 --> 00:02:53,655
An I.D.

42
00:02:53,655 --> 00:02:58,310
stamped by the gateway, out of the agent's reach, was never wrong.

43
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,594
Finding two.

44
00:02:59,594 --> 00:03:03,943
Writing reveals the operator, but not which agent wrote it.

45
00:03:03,943 --> 00:03:10,060
Fingerprints link accounts to their operator with an A U C of zero point nine four.

46
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:20,158
But telling apart that operator's agents is at chance, with forty or a hundred and sixty agents, and with small or frontier models alike.

47
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:23,843
They identify the configuration, not the instance.

48
00:03:23,843 --> 00:03:28,560
Only giving each agent its own memory starts to tell them apart.

49
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,978
Finding three.

50
00:03:29,978 --> 00:03:31,722
Style hides, goals leak.

51
00:03:31,722 --> 00:03:39,063
Rewording every post through another AI makes writing style almost useless for spotting the operator.

52
00:03:39,063 --> 00:03:43,860
But the meaning, what an agent keeps pushing, still gives it away.

53
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:46,543
Finding four, and my key control.

54
00:03:46,543 --> 00:03:52,906
Fingerprints can tell a hidden boss's fronts apart from ordinary companies almost perfectly.

55
00:03:52,906 --> 00:04:03,489
But compared with honest companies that simply agree, they do little better than a coin flip, even when the fronts are shown their score and try to hide.

56
00:04:03,489 --> 00:04:05,564
Text can show a shared agenda.

57
00:04:05,564 --> 00:04:07,570
It cannot prove a conspiracy.

58
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:08,859
Finding five.

59
00:04:08,859 --> 00:04:15,222
With a hundred and sixty agents, automatically merging look-alike accounts made things worse.

60
00:04:15,222 --> 00:04:22,200
Forty-seven of seventy-seven merges were wrong, and overall accuracy fell below using the gateway I.D.

61
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:22,610
alone.

62
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:23,980
A side finding:

63
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:26,113
honest agents mostly pushed back.

64
00:04:26,113 --> 00:04:33,740
Two thirds of their mentions of the fake product were skeptical, and some called out the campaign without being asked.

65
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:36,575
So what should agent builders do?

66
00:04:36,575 --> 00:04:39,453
Take identity out of the agent's hands.

67
00:04:39,453 --> 00:04:43,733
Give every agent copy its own I.D., issued by the gateway.

68
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,651
Read for goals, not style.

69
00:04:45,651 --> 00:04:50,669
And treat fingerprints as leads for human review, never as verdicts.

70
00:04:50,669 --> 00:04:53,842
Everything is open source and reproducible.

71
00:04:53,842 --> 00:04:54,580
Thank you.
